{
    "word": "angiosperm",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e6676abe-82cd-3af7-985d-546f9b8d0a4c",
                "word": "angiosperm",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2175eae6-f57d-4930-af87-28ba71b49e04",
                        "entry_id": "e6676abe-82cd-3af7-985d-546f9b8d0a4c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "angiosperms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f92e35b-e862-33c2-b93d-5a368db02d00",
                        "entry_id": "e6676abe-82cd-3af7-985d-546f9b8d0a4c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any plant of the clade Angiosperms, characterized by having ovules enclosed in an ovary; a flowering plant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46719e40-ffc7-4cfc-aafa-d7504c9c781d",
                                "sense_id": "1f92e35b-e862-33c2-b93d-5a368db02d00",
                                "text": "As with the Lejeuneaceae, this pattern of massive speciation appears to be correlated with the Cretaceous explosion of the angiosperms and the simultaneous creation of a host of new microenvironments, differing in humidity, light intensity, texture, etc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6443aa1-8347-40c6-8a45-cd3ea4bd129b",
                                "sense_id": "1f92e35b-e862-33c2-b93d-5a368db02d00",
                                "text": "The notion of magnoliaceans as the most primitive living angiosperms, justified or not, does not mean that all their characters, including multilacunar nodal anatomy and the lack of tannins, are primary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e091349-f94d-43cd-b67e-291aee060df9",
                                "sense_id": "1f92e35b-e862-33c2-b93d-5a368db02d00",
                                "text": "2009, Xin Wang, 3: New Fossils and New Hope for the Origin of Angiosperms, Pierre Pontarotti, Evolutionary Biology: Concept, Modeling, and Application, page 55,\nWith all these features, it is pretty easy for one to identify an angiosperm. This is a very normal and common practice for neobotanists. However, the situation becomes complicated when you go back to the early history of angiosperms."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4744b417-f22b-4330-ac5b-57219ee97b10",
                                "sense_id": "1f92e35b-e862-33c2-b93d-5a368db02d00",
                                "text": "The palynoassemblage is rich in angiosperm taxa (45.63%) followed by gymnosperms (0.45%), pteridophytes (18.49%) and fungal remains (23.88%)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "75ea041f-7bfa-4ed5-97dd-ba454a131a80",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6676abe-82cd-3af7-985d-546f9b8d0a4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "1f92e35b-e862-33c2-b93d-5a368db02d00",
                        "source_sense_description": "member of plant group",
                        "target_lang_word": "angiosperme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "angiosperme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0488fb71-61c7-3f5d-86a3-2a6a4037e8ce",
                                        "entry_id": "1de4d972-f58b-3a68-ba37-0f5eecf2140a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Plante à fleurs. Représentant du taxon des Magnoliophyta."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cbcf3c2-f3b7-4479-9f1f-3de3e0b4f6a2",
                                                "sense_id": "0488fb71-61c7-3f5d-86a3-2a6a4037e8ce",
                                                "text": "Les seules observations récentes que j’aie faites sur la flore jurassique sont relatives à l’interprétation de certains types de la flore infraliasique ou liasique considérés par quelques paléobotanistes, […], comme des Proangiospermes, c’est à dire des Angiospermes prototypiques, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e182eb2e-6627-4aa4-8268-d67543850aed",
                                                "sense_id": "0488fb71-61c7-3f5d-86a3-2a6a4037e8ce",
                                                "text": "Les Angiospermes ont des modes de dissémination très variés : si nous songeons aux arbres d’abord, nous trouvons les graines légères des Peupliers que le vent transporte au loin grâce à leurs houppes de poils, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "630e419e-0ed1-49cd-b2a8-3ac6b6eebf83",
                                                "sense_id": "0488fb71-61c7-3f5d-86a3-2a6a4037e8ce",
                                                "text": "C'est seulement à la fin du secondaire, à l'époque crétacée qu'apparaissent les angiospermes ou plantes à fleurs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "angiosperme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
