                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "17013574-1f51-48a3-92e5-57511f4651ad",
                                "sense_id": "430297cf-8f8f-3793-8894-a7fc351ef65b",
                                "text": "As with the Lejeuneaceae, this pattern of massive speciation appears to be correlated with the Cretaceous explosion of the angiosperms and the simultaneous creation of a host of new microenvironments, differing in humidity, light intensity, texture, etc.",
                                "translation": "與 Lejeuneaceae 一樣，這種大規模物種形成模式似乎與白堊紀被子植物的爆發以及同時創造出的大量新的微環境有關，這些微環境在濕度、光照強度、紋理等方面各不相同。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e672e62-e90b-4b14-a512-813a44b5e80b",
                                "sense_id": "430297cf-8f8f-3793-8894-a7fc351ef65b",
                                "text": "The notion of magnoliaceans as the most primitive living angiosperms, justified or not, does not mean that all their characters, including multilacunar nodal anatomy and the lack of tannins, are primary.",
                                "translation": "木蘭科植物作為最原始的被子植物，無論合理與否，並不意味著它們的所有特徵，包括多隙節解剖結構和缺乏單寧，都是原始的。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ffc5c1ca-e29e-4fa6-a492-b7c7b5e07723",
                                "sense_id": "430297cf-8f8f-3793-8894-a7fc351ef65b",
                                "text": "With all these features, it is pretty easy for one to identify an angiosperm. This is a very normal and common practice for neobotanists. However, the situation becomes complicated when you go back to the early history of angiosperms."
                            }
                        ]
